-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",395,{
[12609]="7006F2EA\n1\tMeet up with Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur\tGlorfindel suggested you meet at Khanâg Gur north of Damudûr.\n2\tTalk to Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur\tGlorfindel is at Khanâg Gur.\n3\tLook towards the Ordâkhai camp outside Damudûr\030Climb the path south of Khanâg Gur toward Damudûr\tGlorfindel asked you to approach Damudûr and look for some sign of the Thardúth.\n4\tTalk to Ulishár at Khanâg Gur\tUlishár is at Khanâg Gur, waiting to speak with you.\n5\tTalk to Arshûk at Khanâg Gur\tArshûk is at Khanâg Gur.\n6\tTalk to Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur\tGlorfindel is at Khanâg Gur.\n7\tRetrieve a fancy Ordâkhai blade from the camp of Kôth Rau\tGlorfindel believes that if you retrieve a fancy Ordâkhai blade from Kôth Rau, you will convince Arshûk to tell you what he saw.\n8\tBring the fancy Ordâkhai blade to Arshûk at Khanâg Gur\tArshûk is at Khanâg Gur.\n9\tWait for Arshûk to gather his courage\tArshûk gathers his courage.\n10\tTalk to Arshûk at Khanâg Gur\tArshûk is at Khanâg Gur.\n11\tTalk to Ulishár at Khanâg Gur\tUlishár is at Khanâg Gur.\n12\tTalk to Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur\tGlorfindel is at Khanâg Gur.\n",
[12610]="70049624\n1\tDefeat Uruk torturers and destroy torture devices in Naerband\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat Uruk torturers and destroy torture devices in Naerband.\n2\tDefeat Uruk Torturers (total: 6)\030Destroy torture devices (total: 8)\tNaerband is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat Uruk torturers and destroy torture devices in Naerband.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated Uruk torturers and destroyed torture devices in Naerband.\n",
[12611]="70043055\n1\tTalk to Merenir by the centre fountain in Imloth Melui\tMerenir is waiting by the centre fountain in Imloth Melui to speak with you in order to arrange the rescue of Lady Vanyalos.\n2\tTalk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall\tLady Vanyalos has returned to her hall in Imloth Melui.\n",
[12612]="700577C0\n1\tComplete 'A Fondness for Festivity (Intro)'\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three days!\n2\tComplete 'A Fondness for Festivity (Intermediate)'\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n3\tComplete 'A Fondness for Festivity (Advanced)'\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n4\tComplete 'A Fondness for Festivity (Final)'\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three final days!\n5\tTalk to Faeleth in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to Captain Khâtaphos at Furtherholm in the Shield Isles\tYou have participated in countless Midsummer celebrations and spread a great deal of good spirit. You should return to Faeleth in Minas Tirith (Midsummer) or Captain Khâtaphos in Furtherholm.\n",
[12613]="700332FA\n1\tLook north upon Khadar-zarâm\030Look south upon Khadar-zarâm\030Look east from a lower level of Khadar-zarâm\tVantage points for looking out at the Second Hall can be found on the stairs of Khadar-zarâm. You should look out upon the majestic stone trees of the Second Hall, for this is an opportunity to behold some of the finest craftwork of the dwarves from Durin's time. NOTE: This quest requires emotes.\n2\tReturn to Svanr\tSvanr stands upon the stairs of Khadar-zarâm in western Nud-melek. You should return to Svanr.\n",
[12614]="7006C94C\n1\tBring a bucket of water to the tired donkey\tWater seems to be the donkey's most immediate need. There is a bucket of water near the north-eastern fountain in Western Khanâg.\n2\tBring fresh straw to the tired donkey\tYou have given the donkey some refreshing water. Next, you should find some fresh straw and give him something to eat. There is a stack of donkey feed on the north-west side of Western Khanâg.\n3\tGroom the tired donkey\tYou have watered and fed the tired donkey. Next, you should brush the dust from his coat.\n4\tTell the donkey that he is very handsome\tYou have watered, fed, and groomed the tired donkey. Donkeys are social animals. Perhaps you should also talk to him and give him a compliment?\n5\tTalk to Bangud\tYou have done everything you can think of to fulfil the donkey's needs. You should talk to his owner, Bangud, in Western Khanâg.\n",
[12615]="7001A6F9\n1\tUse the draught to strengthen your resolve before entering the pool\tNestawen gave you a draught for your inventory that will protect you against the fell lights that gently sap life from all around. Nestawen wants you to sip from the tincture she made so that you will be strengthened against the bog-lights.\n2\tDefeat bog-lights (total: 18)\tThe sickly pool is just to the south of Estolad Mernael. Nestawen wants you to drive away the bog-lights that reside in the Drownholt and has provided you with a draught that will protect you against the dire effects of the water.\n3\tTalk to Nestawen at Estolad Mernael\tNestawen is at Estolad Mernael, north of the sickly pool. You should return to Nestawen at once and inform her of your success against the fell lights in the pool.\n",
[12616]="7002D06F\n1\tTalk to Swithulf\tSwithulf is at the tower near the farmstead. Gadda wants you to speak with his friend Swithulf and learn what transpires at the tower.\n",
[12617]="7003EA7A\n1\tSearch the gate-house of Isengard for Orcs\tThe gate-house can be found inside the southern entrance of Isengard. Quickbeam wants you to search what remains of Isengard for any sign of Orcs.\n2\tSearch the ring of Isengard for Orcs\030Search the flooded tents and wreckage for Orcs\030Search Orthanc's doorway for Orcs\tThe remains of the ring of Isengard can be found surrounding Orthanc in northern Nan Curunír. You have searched the gate-house and should now search the flooded ring of Isengard for any sign of Orcs or other foes.\n3\tSearch the depths of Isengard for Orcs\tThe entrance to the depths of Isengard can be found through the door to the north of Orthanc. You have searched all that remains above ground in Isengard, but you should search the depths before returning to Quickbeam.\n4\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found across the river Isen outside the eastern side of Isengard. You have thoroughly searched the ruins of Isengard and found only wounded and slain foes. You should return to Quickbeam.\n",
[12618]="70030A14\n1\tSpeak with Etta and hear her counsel\tEtta is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should speak with Etta and hear her opinion.\n2\tSoldiers of Floodwend can be found guarding the three gates of the town.\t\n3\tClimb the tower behind the Mead Hall and look to the forest\tThere is a tower behind the Floodwend Mead Hall that offers a view of the forest. You should climb the tower and look for something unusual. You must perform an emote to advance this quest.\n4\tReturn to Thane Radwig\tRadwig, Thane of Floodwend, awaits you in the Mead Hall. You should speak with Radwig and tell him of the information you gathered.\n5\tSpeak with Etta\tEtta is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should speak with Etta.\n",
[12619]="7005718C\n1\tDefeat trolls in Misthallow (total: 6)\tTrolls can be found in Misthallow. You should defeat trolls in Misthallow.\n2\tTalk to Léothred at Thokvist\tLéothred can be found at Thokvist. You should talk to Léothred.\n",
[12620]="70042F5B\n1\tPatrol the Great Bridge of Osgiliath\tThe Great Bridge crosses over the Anduin in central Osgiliath. Meldir has asked you to investigate how the host of Minas Morgul is ferrying siege equipment across the once-broken bridge.\n2\tTalk to Meldir\tMeldir can be found along the south-western walls of Osgiliath. You have discovered a great, crude span that can bear the weight of siege equipment now covering the ruined Great Bridge. You should return to Meldir.\n",
[12621]="70058FC9\n1\tPlant banners of the Gabil'akkâ on the march to Gundabad (total: 7)\tGood locations for banners can be found along the path to Mount Gundabad in the War of Three Peaks. Glóin has asked you to plant banners of the Gabil'akkâ across the War of Three Peaks as you march to Mount Gundabad. NOTE: It is recommended that you complete this quest as you adventure across the War of Three Peaks.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have planted banners of Gabil'akkâ across the War of Three Peaks.\n",
[12622]="70046BBA\n1\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found in after-battle Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Angbor\tYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.\n3\tSeek out Thurindol in North Ithilien\tYou should talk to Thurindol, who can be found in North Ithilien near the after-battle Cross-roads.\n",
[12623]="70046B1E\n1\tSearch for Rangers in Osgiliath\tSearch for Rangers of Ithilien within after-battle Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Arodor\030Talk to Gladhir\030Talk to Mírthel\tGladhir, Mírthel, and Arodor can be found at the main Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath. You should speak with the other Rangers.\n3\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the main Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n",
[12624]="70046BB2\n1\tTravel to the Cross-roads\tYou should travel to the Cross-roads, which lie east of after-battle Osgiliath.\n2\tTalk to Angbor at the Cross-roads\tYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.\n3\tLook at Statue of the Fallen King\tView the statue at the after-battle Cross-roads.\n4\tTalk to Angbor\tYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads.\n",
[12625]="7003E736\n1\tTalk to Ringhul\tRinghul is at his post in the High Moor, far to the north and east of Echad Candelleth. Candelleth bade you speak with Ringhul, marchwarden of the High Moor, to gain entrance into Rivendell.\n",
[12626]="70059322\n1\tThe market stalls of potential vendors have been set up in Trestlebridge. You should inspect the produce of the farmers.\t\n2\tInspect the final market stall\tThe market stalls of potential vendors have been set up in Trestlebridge. You should inspect the produce of the farmers.\n3\tTalk to the helpful vendor\tThe market stalls of potential vendors have been set up in Trestlebridge. You should talk to the farmer closest to the stall with the rancid fruit.\n4\tYou should follow in pursuit of the fleeing vendor\030Find and follow the man's trail\tThe owner of the poisonous fruit ran out of town and towards the Wildwood. You should follow in pursuit and try to catch up with this man.\n5\tConfront the troublesome brigand\tThe vendor can be found outside of Cotfast in the Wildwood. You should confront the vendor.\n6\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n7\tSurvey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge\tReconstruction work continues on Trestlebridge. You should survey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge.\n8\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n",
[12627]="700460B7\n1\tFind patients suffering from the Black Shadow in the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest, and mark them for Aragorn.\t\n2\tReturn to Aragorn\tAragorn stands in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Return to Aragorn and let him know that you have marked out those suffering from the Black Shadow.\n",
[12628]="7002651F\n1\tDefeat the Master of Beasts\tThe Master of Beasts resides in the caves of western Nan Curunír. Ondor instructed you to defeat the Master of Beasts.\n2\tTalk to Ondor in Nan Curunír\tOndor is encamped near the caves of western Nan Curunír. You should tell Ondor that you have defeated the Master of Beasts.\n",
[12629]="7005B189\n1\tFind and defeat the strange Orc leading Azog's forces at Kamaz-kala\tHurákh can be found at Kamaz-kala. You should find and defeat Hurákh at Kamaz-kala.\n2\tFind and defeat Hurákh at Kamaz-kala\tHurákh can be found at Kamaz-kala. You should find and defeat Hurákh at Kamaz-kala.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Hurákh.\n",
[12630]="7004CE26\n1\tMake your way to the Master's manor\tSomething is amiss in Lake-town. You should make your way to the Master's manor.\n2\tTalk to the guard at the Master's manor\tSomething is amiss in Lake-town. You should talk to the guard at the Master's manor.\n3\tTalk to Mervárth\tMervárth can be found near the Master's manor. You should talk to Mervárth.\n",
[12631]="70058C8F\n1\tFind some sign of Bandrauth Adder-fang in Tûr Ágal\tBandrauth Adder-fang can be found within Tûr Ágal at Caivád Sâr. Múta has asked you to find and defeat the Angmarim sorcerer, Bandrauth Adder-fang, in Tûr Ágal. You should search the tower for any sign of him.\n2\tExamine the pedestal and remain ready to confront Bandrauth Adder-fang\tThe dusty pedestal can be found in the highest chamber of Tûr Ágal. You have not found Bandrauth Adder-fang, but you have discovered a curious, dusty pedestal inscribed with Angmarim runes. You should examine the pedestal more closely.\n3\tTalk to Múta at Caivád Sâr\tMúta can be found outside Caivád Sâr in northern Elderslade. You wounded Bandrauth Adder-fang, but he was able to escape from his encounter with you. You should return to Múta and inform her of what has happened.\n",
[12632]="7001D137\n1\tSummon and defeat the morvul-guard\tThe master of the morvul-slaves can be summoned in Dannenglor, north of the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. You should use the merrevail's horn to summon the morvul-guard.\n2\tTalk to Puiguil in the Haunted Inn\tPuiguil can be found in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor. You should return with news of your success to Puiguil.\n",
[12633]="7001BFC7\n1\tDefeat the Master of the Ruins\tThe Master of the Ruins wanders within the ruins of Nan Dhelu, north of Dol Vaeg. Cwendreda warned you to be cautious while searching Nan Dhelu for the Master of the Ruins and offered you a reward should you defeat the monster.\n2\tTalk to Cwendreda at Dol Vaeg\tCwendreda is at Dol Vaeg. Cwendreda awaits your return and the news that the Master of the Ruins has been defeated.\n",
[12634]="7004D070\n1\tTalk to Stafhild\tStafhild can be found in the unruly group in Lake-town. You should hear what Stafhild has to say.\n2\tFind the Master of Lake-town\tFind the Master of Lake-town.\n3\tComplete 'The Master's Murder' quest arc\tYou should assist the Men of Lake-town. The Trail of Rust quest arc will continue after completing The Master's Murder quest arc which begins with the Lake-town guard in front of the Master's manor in Lake-town.\n4\tTalk to Dagrun\tYou should speak with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's Manor in Lake-town.\n5\tTalk to Dagrun again\tYou should speak some more with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.\n6\tComplete 'A Question of Bloodline'\030Complete 'Underbelly of Deceit'\tDagrun can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town. You should assist Dagrun with her troubles.\n7\tTalk to the crowd gathered outside the manor about Smaug's bones\tA crowd of people are gathered outside of the Master's manor in Lake-town. With Dagrun's reputation improved, now would be a good time to speak to the Men of Lake-town about Smaug's bones, on behalf of the Master.\n8\tTalk to Dagrun\tYou should speak with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.\n",
[12635]="7005266D\n1\tSearch near Bag End for the suspicious figure\tWaldo Rumble saw a strange figure lurking near the Party Tree during the early morning hours, but it fled up the Hill toward Bag End when he approached.\n2\tPick up the discarded scroll near Bag End\tA small scroll has fallen by the path near Bag End. It seems to be very similar to the cards hanging on the Party Tree.\n3\tTalk to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins\tLobelia Sackville-Baggins has called you over, clearly intending to give you a piece of her mind.\n4\tBring the discarded scroll to Waldo Rumble by the Party Tree\tWaldo Rumble is by the Party Tree, waiting for some clue to the identity of the suspicious figure he saw.\n5\tFollow the clues in the scroll to solve the mystery\tYou have in your possession a mysterious scroll that may contain a clue to learning the identity of the mysterious party-planner who festooned the Party Tree with ribbons and cards.\n6\tFollow the clues in the scroll to solve the mystery\tYou have in your possession a mysterious scroll that may contain a clue to learning the identity of the mysterious party-planner who festooned the Party Tree with ribbons and cards.\n7\tFollow the clues in the scroll to solve the mystery\tYou have in your possession a mysterious scroll that may contain a clue to learning the identity of the mysterious party-planner who festooned the Party Tree with ribbons and cards.\n8\tFollow the clues in the scroll to solve the mystery\tYou have in your possession a mysterious scroll that may contain a clue to learning the identity of the mysterious party-planner who festooned the Party Tree with ribbons and cards.\n9\tFollow the clues in the scroll to solve the mystery\tYou have in your possession a mysterious scroll that may contain a clue to learning the identity of the mysterious party-planner who festooned the Party Tree with ribbons and cards.\n10\tTalk to Ebrulf Sackville\tYou found Ebrulf Sackville by a pile of scrolls north-west of Overhill, in the Bindbole Wood. Is he responsible for the shenanigans that have so preoccupied the thoughts of Waldo Rumble and the Party Planning Committee?\n11\tTalk to Waldo Rumble by the Party Tree\tYou have learned the identity of the mastermind behind the cards hanging from the Party Tree and should return now to Waldo Rumble.\n",
[12636]="7000325D\n1\tCollect Silver Tusk-ring (total: 3)\tMammoths can be found throughout the Misty Mountains, but especially in areas where giants walk. Golhador has expressed concern that the mammoths and the giants have formed an alliance and asked you to bring the silver tusk-rings worn by the mammoths for him to examine.\n2\tBring silver tusk-rings to Golhador\tGolhador is at the High Crag camp. Golhador is waiting for you to return with tusk-rings that might illuminate the nature of the alliance between the mammoths and the giants of the Misty Mountains.\n",
[12637]="7003FE69\n1\tCollect supplies (total: 7)\tThe supplies should be commandeered before the corsairs can use them.\n",
[12638]="7000D50B\n1\tTalk to Tasgall and travel to Nád Nathair\tTasgall's camp-site is north of Aughaire and south-east of Nád Nathair. Tasgall is waiting to travel with you in search of Bangrath and Murragrath.\n2\tTalk to Tasgall\tTasgall's camp-site is north of Aughaire and south-east of Nád Nathair. You and Tasgall were successful in your hunt of Bangrath and Murragrath. He is waiting to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Rona\tRona is at the centre island of Aughaire, east of Crannog's ruling-seat. Tasgall has been satisfied with the aid you lent him and wants you to tell his sister Rona that he will soon return to the settlement.\n",
[12639]="7006C505\n1\tDefeat spiders (total: 10)\tYour mission is to kill spiders in Ushbarab and slay the Matron of the Fang when she emerges to defend her nest.\n2\tDefeat the Matron of the Fang\tFind and defeat the Matron of the Fang in Ushbarab.\n",
[12640]="70062975\n1\tDismantle the bed\tRhiangar has asked for your help dismantling her father's bed so that it can be moved downstairs. The Mayor's bed is in the Mayor's home, in Herne.\n2\tReassemble the Mayor's bed\tYou have dismantled the bed in the upstairs room of the Mayor's house. Now you should reassemble it downstairs, in his office. The Mayor's office is in his home in Herne.\n3\tTalk to Rhiangar\tYou should let Rhiangar know that you have moved her father's bed into the library. Rhiangar is in the kitchen in the Mayor's house in Herne.\n",
})
